## Expert Summary

A rose gold radiant cut engagement ring is one of the smartest and most photogenic combinations in the current certified diamond market.

Rose gold masks color. Buy G or H instead of D-F — save $700–$2,000 per carat with zero visible difference face-up. The blush warmth of rose gold makes G-H a positive match, not a budget compromise. This single rule alone can dramatically change what ring you can build.

The radiant cut has 70 facets — more than any comparable fancy shape. In rose gold's blush-toned light, those 70 facets scatter a fire that no other metal produces.

It is softer than yellow gold fire. Warmer than white gold fire. Uniquely romantic, and consistently the most photographed engagement ring fire character in current bridal media.

